// A `while` loop inside a `syntax` rule's `quote { .. }` must keep its
// condition. Today the condition is lost: the checker reports QUOTE003 for
// the `$n` it held, and the loop has no exit (LOOP005). `loop { if .. {
// break; } .. }` works in its place (found building PROP-009 step 1a).
//
// Expected output, worked by hand: count_to(3) prints i = 0, 1, 2 and
// stops when i < 3 fails at i = 3.
pub syntax {
    count_to(n) => quote { {
        var i = 0;
        while i < $n {
            print(i);
            i = i + 1;
        }
    } };
}

fn main() {
    count_to(3);
}
